Experimental source-owned telemetry exclusion; not automatically applied by Context Foundry.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006 bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires prior caller/auth/refusal/restricted/catalog/settings/empty-auth/presence patches.
Modules: telemetry-export::{ownStartupTelemetry,initTelemetryExport,retireStartupTelemetry};
main CLI explicit flag; sdk exact-session binding; CLI args/flag table.
Tests: startup-telemetry-owner.test.ts, telemetry-export.test.ts, original auth,
presence, settings, caller, main/CLI and restricted SDK suites.
Difference: --startup-no-telemetry requires --restrict-tools; it installs a source
owner before CLI initialization, refuses enabled or repeated work before exporter
construction, joins the original disabled call and completion observer, and binds
retirement to the exact sealed session/registry after original presence retirement.
Ordinary telemetry outside the flag remains available. This does not establish a
blanket network fence, direct OTLP imports, general exporter drain, complete startup
inventory, Ready, paid execution, signing or release acceptance.

